// expect-error: '*' operands must be numeric; got 'String' and 'String'
// p46 — String * String must be a clean Sema rejection, not an
// LLVM IR "Integer arithmetic operators only work with integral
// types" crash (v3.0.3, surfaced by tools/fuzz.py @ seed=1; again in
// v6.0.1 @ seed=7 via `"x" * 16.0.sqrt().str()`).
//
// Cause (v6.0.2): Sema's operator-overload branch found
// `String.__mul(self, n: Int)` for a String left operand and accepted
// the expression without checking the right operand against `n: Int`,
// so the numeric gate below never ran and Codegen emitted
// `mul %String*, %String*`. The branch now checks the right operand:
// builtin (extern) overloads fall through to their own operand rules
// on a mismatch — `"n=" + 5` still concatenates — and user-defined
// overloads report the mismatch directly.
//
// Until v6.0.1 this probe couldn't express the rejection (probes had to
// compile); `// expect-error:` lets it lock the exact diagnostic.

define main() -> void {
    print("-" * 3)        // legal: String * Int repetition
    print("a" * "b")      // Q0201: operands must be numeric
}
